+# Anaadi brand kit (draft for review, 21 Nov 2026)
+
+## Picks
+- Profile picture: anaadi-logo-navy-800.png (the gold "అ" sun ring, recoloured from purple to the episodes' deep navy). Old purple version kept as anaadi-logo-800.png.
+- Banner: anaadi-banner-nano-banana-2560x1440.jpg (devas vs asuras, same painted look as the episodes; the name sits inside YouTube's mobile safe area, checked in preview-banner-nano-banana.jpg).
+- Not picked: anaadi-banner-2560x1440.jpg and the devas-rakshasas banner use the older code-drawn characters, which no longer match the episodes.
+
+## Look (keep every Short, thumbnail and post on this)
+- Background: deep cosmic navy #02101F to #102E3F, small stars.
+- Accent: temple gold #E8B04A (titles, rings, glows). Light text: #F3E9D2.
+- Art: the Gemini painted flat-vector style of episodes 1 and 2, warm golden light on the god, dark water or sky around.
+- Titles: Telugu in Ramabhadra (bold, gold), English small caps in a serif, e.g. "ANAADI".
+- Episode card: "భాగం N" in gold at the start, the gold ring from the logo behind it.
+
+## Channel description (paste into YouTube > Customise channel > Basic info)
+అనాది అంటే ఆది లేనిది. సృష్టి ఆరంభం నుంచి మన పురాణాలు, ఇతిహాసాల కథలను వరుసగా, ఒక్కో నిమిషం వీడియోలో, సరళమైన తెలుగులో చెబుతాం. భాగం 1 నుంచి చూడండి.
+
+Anaadi means "that which has no beginning". The Puranas and the epics told in story order, from the creation onward, one minute at a time, in simple Telugu. Start from part 1.
+
+## Channel keywords (Settings > Channel > Basic info)
+anaadi, telugu mythology, puranalu, telugu stories, srishti, vishnu, brahma, bhagavatam, indian mythology shorts, itihasa
