+    { "say": "On Friday, the FAA held departures at every airport in the US." },
+    { "say": "The reason: communication problems at several of its big air traffic control centers." },
+    { "say": "Towers only handle takeoffs and landings. In between, huge regional centers guide the planes." },
+    { "say": "Each center sees planes through faraway radar sites, and talks to pilots through faraway radio sites." },
+    { "say": "All of that reaches the center over telecom lines. If they fail, controllers can lose the picture, or the voice." },
+    { "say": "So the safe move is a ground stop. New flights wait at the gate." },
+    { "say": "Planes already flying keep going and land. Fewer planes means less to watch while systems are down." },
+    { "say": "The FAA hasn't said exactly what broke. Outages like this usually start with a cut cable or a failed network box." },
+    { "say": "Flights restart as centers recover. But planes and crews are stuck in the wrong cities, so cancellations spill into the next day." },
+    { "hold": 3.4 }
+  ],
+  "card": { "lines": ["FOLLOW FOR HOW THINGS WORK,", "IN A MINUTE."] }
+}
